==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AdminCannotAccessClinicalContent  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AdminCannotAccessClinicalContent.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows Alloy to construct a world where a HospitalAdministrator AccessAttempt has outcome=Permitted on RecordLookup or AddNote. LeastPrivilege requires all Permitted outcomes to respect the matrix (which excludes HospitalAdministrator from clinical ops), and FR_005_AdminNoClinicAccess directly asserts this cannot happen.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_005_AdminNoClinicAccess, FR_018_AdminContentBlindness
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_005_AdminNoClinicAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_018_AdminContentBlindness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets Alloy construct an AccessAttempt with outcome=Permitted on a clinical endpoint without any CareTeamMembership linking the caller to the patient. OwnershipBasedAccess and FR_004_CareTeamGating both assert this is impossible; the injection forces exactly that structure.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEntryBelongsToOneAttempt  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditEntryBelongsToOneAttempt.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a single AuditEntry to be shared by two distinct AccessAttempts, simulating a mutated or overwritten audit row. FR_014_AuditImmutability requires every AuditEntry to have exactly one parent attempt; the injection makes two attempts share one entry.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, AuditCompleteness, FR_014_AuditImmutability
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_AuditImmutability: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteCreatedByOneAttempt  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_NoteCreatedByOneAttempt.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a ClinicalNote to appear as the aaCreatedNote of two distinct AccessAttempts, simulating an update/edit of an existing note. AppendOnly and FR_011_NotesAppendOnly assert each note is produced by at most one attempt.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_011_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditRoleSnapshotMatchesCaller  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditRoleSnapshotMatchesCaller.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows an AuditEntry to carry a role snapshot that does not match the accessor's actual role, simulating misattribution. AttributionCorrectness asserts the snapshot must equal the accessor's userRole.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_013_AuditRoleSnapshotValid
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditRoleSnapshotValid: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AdminOnlyListAudit  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AdminOnlyListAudit.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a clinical-role AccessAttempt to obtain Permitted on ListAudit, violating the administrator-only gate. FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditEndpoint asserts clinical roles never receive Permitted on this endpoint; the injection forces exactly that.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditEndpoint
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditEndpoint: PASS (vacuous?)

